# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# What this .gitignore protects:
#
# ✅ COMMITTED (so anyone cloning gets a working starting state):
#    - All source files, config, scripts, docs
#    - Empty template versions of applications-log.csv, seen-jobs.csv,
#      session-state.json (just headers / empty JSON — no personal data)
#    - Placeholder folders (Resume/, cover-letters/, browser-profile/)
#      via .gitkeep so the directory structure exists on clone
#
# ❌ NOT COMMITTED (would either bloat the repo or leak personal data):
#    - node_modules/  → huge, auto-generated by `npm install`
#    - Your resume    → personal
#    - browser-profile/ contents → contains your LinkedIn cookies + Google
#      session. Committing these would let anyone log in as you. NEVER push.
#    - Generated cover letters → per-job, per-user output
#    - ats-accounts.txt → may contain account/email info
#    - Screenshots and debug artifacts
#
# Note: once you start running the agent, applications-log.csv / seen-jobs.csv
# / session-state.json will get personal data appended. Those committed files
# are *template starting states* — don't push your modified versions unless you
# explicitly want your job-application history in a public repo.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Dependencies — regenerated by `npm install`
node_modules/

# Personal resume — recipients drop their own into Resume/
Resume/*.pdf
Resume/*.docx
*Resume*.pdf
*Resume*.docx
*resume*.pdf
*resume*.docx

# Per-user runtime state that may contain sensitive info
ats-accounts.txt
scheduled-runs.log

# Local env overrides (optional helper config). No secrets are required — the
# refine helper uses the claude CLI, not an API key — but ignore .env anyway.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Generated cover letters (per-job, per-user)
cover-letters/*.txt
cover-letters/*.md
!cover-letters/.gitkeep

# Persistent browser profiles — contain LinkedIn cookies, Google session,
# ATS logins. NEVER commit. Base folder tracked via .gitkeep.
# Covers every per-identity profile + backups:
#   browser-profile-<persona>   one per persona, derived in src/personas.js
# Nothing else should appear here — an invented profile name is how this repo
# once accumulated 23 profile directories and 5 GB of disk.
#   *.saved / *.bak snapshots
browser-profile/*
!browser-profile/.gitkeep
browser-profile-*/

# Quarantined orphan profiles awaiting deletion (see .profile-archive/README.txt)
.profile-archive/

# Playwright MCP scratch
.playwright-mcp/

# Local Claude Code settings (per-user)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Screenshots / debug artifacts
*.png
*.jpeg
*.jpg

# Run artifacts. These now land in .state/runs/ (owner-only 0700) via
# src/core/paths.js, but SCRATCH can still redirect batch logs here, and these
# files carry PII: a batch log opens with "Persona: <name> <email>" and then lists
# every job URL evaluated. Previously untracked AND unignored, so a `git add -A`
# would have committed them.
*-nbatch-*.log
*-batch-*.log
dryrun-*.png

# Local recovery backups created during runs (not the source of truth — the live
# seen-jobs.csv / applications-log.csv are). Keep the repo clean of these.
*.bak.csv
*.backup.csv
*.backup2.csv
*.backup.json
*.bak.json
# Ad-hoc snapshot names slipped the patterns above — seen-jobs.retrybak.csv was
# tracked with 1,953 real rows because it matches neither *.bak.csv nor
# *.backup.csv. Catch any bak/backup snapshot of the history files.
*bak*.csv
*bak*.json
*backup*.csv
*backup*.json
*.bak-*
.DS_Store
dryrun-*.txt

# Claude Code skills — the apply-agent skill lives in ~/.claude/skills (personal,
# account-level) because it carries REAL identity data (names, emails, phones,
# resume paths). This repo is public: never commit a skill directory here.
.claude/

# Owner-only agent state: NDJSON ledgers, attention/friction queues, rounds,
# autonomy grants, and the file-backed profile fallback. Contains real
# application history — never commit.
.state/
data/agent-config.json
